  "title": "Radar - CVE pages in Zero Wire",
  "content": "<p><a href=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/radar/\"><strong>Cloudflare Radar</strong></a> <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Zero Wire<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a> now has a page for every published CVE. Each page brings together what you need to decide how urgently to act on a vulnerability: how severe it is, whether it is being exploited, what it affects, and how to fix it.</p>\n<img alt=\"Animation searching the CVE list for log4j, filtering to Critical severity, sorting by highest score, and opening the Log4Shell CVE page, then scrolling through all of its sections, from exploitation to references\" height=\"900\" src=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/image/onerror=redirect,width=1600,height=900,format=webp/_astro/radar-zero-wire-cves.EBDpI3NT.webp\" width=\"1600\" />\n<div class=\"heading-wrapper level-h4\" tabindex=\"-1\"><h4 id=\"browse-cves\">Browse CVEs</h4><a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#browse-cves\"><span class=\"anchor-icon\"><svg height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\" fill=\"currentcolor\"></path></svg></span></a></div>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CVE list<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a> includes every published CVE. Sort them by date or CVSS score, search by CVE ID or keyword, such as a product or vendor name, and filter by severity and year. Each row shows the CVE's score and highlights CVEs in the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog and those with a fix available.</p>\n<div class=\"heading-wrapper level-h4\" tabindex=\"-1\"><h4 id=\"cve-pages\">CVE pages</h4><a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#cve-pages\"><span class=\"anchor-icon\"><svg height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\" fill=\"currentcolor\"></path></svg></span></a></div>\n<p>Each CVE page, such as <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves/CVE-2021-44228\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell)<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a>, starts with its CVSS score, description, and key dates, followed by:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Exploitation</strong>: whether the CVE is in the CISA KEV catalog, including known ransomware use, the CISA SSVC assessment, and the FIRST EPSS probability of exploitation.</li>\n<li><strong>Affected products</strong>: the affected vendors, products, and versions, as listed by the organization that published the CVE and by NVD.</li>\n<li><strong>Recommended actions</strong>: how to fix the vulnerability, or reduce the risk until you can, including CISA's guidance for known exploited CVEs.</li>\n<li><strong>Severity</strong>: every CVSS score for the CVE, with each metric explained.</li>\n<li><strong>Weaknesses and attack patterns</strong>: the related CWE weaknesses and CAPEC attack patterns.</li>\n<li><strong>References</strong>: advisories, patches, and other sources.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>CVEs cited in <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Zero Wire briefings<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a> link to their CVE pages, and each CVE page links back to the briefings that cite it.</p>\n<div class=\"heading-wrapper level-h4\" tabindex=\"-1\"><h4 id=\"search-and-follow\">Search and follow</h4><a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#search-and-follow\"><span class=\"anchor-icon\"><svg height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\" fill=\"currentcolor\"></path></svg></span></a></div>\n<p>Search for a CVE ID or keyword from anywhere on Radar, using the search bar or Cmd+K (Ctrl+K on Windows and Linux), to jump straight to a CVE page.</p>\n<img alt=\"Radar search showing CVE results for log4j\" height=\"1620\" src=\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/image/onerror=redirect,width=2880,height=1620,format=webp/_astro/radar-zero-wire-cves-search.B09HTzyf.webp\" width=\"2880\" />\n<p>To follow new CVEs, subscribe to the <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves/feed\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">RSS<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a>, <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves/feed?format=atom\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Atom<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a>, or <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves/feed?format=json\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">JSON<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a> feed. Each feed can be filtered by severity, such as the feed of <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves/feed?severity=critical\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Critical CVEs<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a>.</p>\n<p>Explore the <a href=\"https://radar.cloudflare.com/zero-wire/cves\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">CVE list<span class=\"external-link\"> ↗︎</span></a> on Cloudflare Radar.</p>",
